menuconfig CTLV
	tristate "CTLV character device TLV UAPI"
	# A blob attr may name a dma-buf, whatever family declares one.
	select DMA_SHARED_BUFFER
	help
	  CTLV provides character device UAPIs described by a checked-in YAML
	  specification. It owns the character device lifetime, the strict TLV
	  message format, request validation, reply serialization, the large
	  payloads a request describes rather than carries, per-open event
	  queues and runtime schema introspection, so families only implement
	  semantics.

	  If you don't know what to do here, say N.

if CTLV

config CTLV_KUNIT_TEST
	tristate "CTLV metadata KUnit tests" if !KUNIT_ALL_TESTS
	depends on KUNIT
	default KUNIT_ALL_TESTS
	help
	  Checks the generated schema metadata of every family in this tree
	  against the rules the core relies on without re-checking them at
	  runtime: node indices that stay inside their array, children that are
	  contiguous with the required ones first, IDs composed of the declared
	  parts, and message lengths that agree with the wire arithmetic. The
	  schema tool's own fixture families are built in for this, so that
	  every shape the schema language allows is covered.

	  The tests are a module of their own, ctlv-kunit, and run when it is
	  loaded, or during boot when it is built in.

	  If you are unsure, say N.

config CTLV_TEST
	tristate "CTLV test device"
	depends on CTLV
	select DEBUG_FS
	help
	  A CTLV family with no hardware behind it, implementing ctlv-test so
	  that the kselftests in tools/testing/selftests/ctlv/ can drive CTLV
	  from userspace.
	  Every op it answers exists because a test needs that exact shape, so
	  some of them behave badly on purpose.

	  Its debugfs directory controls which devices exist and arranges an
	  op's test conditions.

	  If you are unsure, say N.

config CTLV_TEST_CHILD
	tristate "CTLV test device of an inheriting family"
	depends on CTLV_TEST
	help
	  The same, for the ctlv-test-child family, which inherits ctlv-test
	  and adds one op of its own. A separate module, so that the selftests
	  cover an inheritance chain crossing a module boundary, with a debugfs
	  directory of its own.

	  If you are unsure, say N.

endif # CTLV
